.SH NAME
import\-ferm \- import existing firewall rules into ferm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBimport\-ferm\fR > ferm.conf
.PP
iptables\-save | \fBimport\-ferm\fR > ferm.conf
.PP
\&\fBimport\-ferm\fR \fIinputfile\fR > ferm.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This script helps you with porting an existing IPv4 firewall
configuration to ferm.  It reads a file generated with
\&\fBiptables\-save\fR, and tries to suggest a ferm configuration file.
.PP
If no input file was specified on the command line, \fBimport\-ferm\fR
reads a dump piped into standard input, or, when standard input is a
terminal, runs \fIiptables\-save\fR itself.  A bare \f(CW\*(C`\-\*(C'\fR as \fIinputfile\fR
reads standard input explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR" 12
.IX Item "-h, --help"
Print the usage banner and exit.  Any other option\-like argument (a dash followed by more characters) is a usage error: \fBimport\-ferm\fR takes only input files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
.IP \fBFERM_DOMAIN\fR 12
.IX Item "FERM_DOMAIN"
The domain the imported rules belong to: \f(CW\*(C`ip\*(C'\fR (default) or \f(CW\*(C`ip6\*(C'\fR.  Set \f(CW\*(C`FERM_DOMAIN=ip6\*(C'\fR when feeding an \fBip6tables\-save\fR\|(8) dump.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
iptables\-save older than 1.3 is unable to write valid saves \- this is
not a bug in \fBimport\-ferm\fR.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBferm\fR\|(1)
